    isbefore: []  # 864b
    duplicate_of: []  # 864b
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 864b
    pr_ref:  # 864b
    description: "META invariant for the cross-language `linkers/inherited_calls.py` campaign (5 PRs, sequential). Canonical plan at `~/puluf-plan.md` (Alternative B post-WI-puluf design).\n\n**Architecture.** Analyzer→linker contract extended via three optional `make_unresolved_edge` kwargs (`enclosing_class`, `receiver_type_hint`, `inherited_field_receiver`) that land in `Edge.meta`. Existing emit sites unchanged at default. Java/Ruby analyzers opt in to emit hints; the linker walks ancestor chains to resolve.\n\nPer-language MRO dispatch table `_MRO_WALKERS: dict[str, Callable]` lives in `linkers/inherited_calls.py`. Hardcoded clauses (YAML and decorator-hooks rejected as ceremony for static language semantics). Initial walkers: `_walk_single_then_interfaces` (Java/Kotlin/C#/Scala-class — default fallback), `_walk_insertion_order` (Ruby/Groovy), `_walk_c3` (Python), `_walk_left_to_right` (PHP/Swift/Obj-C/C++), `_walk_linearization` (Scala traits). Depth cap = 10 (matches existing Java+Ruby walks).\n\nLinker registers at `priority=18` (between `inheritance`=15 and `type_hierarchy`=20). Requires extracting `_TypeHierarchyIndex` build into a module-public `build_method_index()` helper in `type_hierarchy.py` so `inherited_calls` reuses it without a circular ordering dependency. `LinkerActivation(always=True)`. `LinkerRequirement(name=\"unresolved_edges_with_hints\")` reports diagnostics when no analyzer emits hints.\n\n**Children (chained `isbefore`, all tagged `cross_language_parity`, all carry `awaits_bakeoff_validation` at merge):**\n- WI-a (PR-1): Contract + shared helpers — pure additive refactor\n- WI-b (PR-2): Linker substrate + Ruby migration + WI-puluf closure\n- WI-c (PR-3): Java Site 1 lift\n- WI-d (PR-4): Java analyzer enrichment for Sites 2/3 (meta only, unconsumed)\n- WI-e (PR-5): Java Sites 2+3 lift (linker consumes PR-4 meta)\n\n**Status lifecycle:** `violated` at file time → `pending_validation` when PR-5 merges → `satisfied` after one full BROAD cycle confirms no regression across spring-petclinic + chatwoot + hypergumbo-self.\n\n**Closure criterion.** All 5 PRs merged; Java analyzer ~250 LOC deleted (three inherited-walk sites); Ruby analyzer ~80 LOC deleted (`_find_inherited_initialize`); new `linkers/inherited_calls.py` ~280 LOC; Total Java+Ruby behavior preserved (edge-set identity check); new `includes` edges visible in Ruby behavior maps; Sidekiq / ActiveModel / Concern method dispatch visible on chatwoot.\n\n**Deferred follow-up META** (file after PR-5 closes): \"Inherited-call parity across all 12 silent-gap analyzers (Python, Kotlin, Scala, PHP, C#, C++, Go, Swift, Obj-C, Groovy, Rust, JS/TS).\" Sibling WIs one-per-language, all `todo_soft` someday. Activated only when a bakeoff dead-code FP traces to missing inheritance coverage in that language."  # 864b
    fields:  # 864b
      statement: "All inheritance-aware call resolution MUST be performed by the Tier-2 Infrastructure linker `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/inherited_calls.py`. Language analyzers MUST emit only `make_unresolved_edge(...)` with optional hints (`enclosing_class`, `receiver_type_hint`, `inherited_field_receiver`) on `Edge.meta`, and MUST NOT walk ancestor chains themselves to resolve `calls` edges. The linker owns per-language MRO walking (Java/Kotlin/C#/Scala-class: single-then-interfaces; Ruby/Groovy: insertion-order; Python: C3; PHP/Swift/Obj-C/C++: left-to-right; Scala traits: linearization). Edge types preserved from Java/Ruby precedent: `evidence_type=\"ast_call_inherited\"` (Site 1, conf 0.90), `ast_call_inherited_method` (Site 2, conf 0.70), `ast_call_inherited_field` (Site 3, conf 0.80). New `edge_type=\"includes\"` with `evidence_type=\"ast_includes\"` for Ruby `include`/`extend`, emitted from extended `inheritance.py`."  # 864b
      root_cause: "Inheritance-aware call resolution is duplicated in 2 of 14 analyzers: Java (`java.py:1414-1591`, three sites emitting `ast_call_inherited` / `ast_call_inherited_method` / `ast_call_inherited_field`) and Ruby (`ruby.py:1901-1956`, `_find_inherited_initialize`). The other 12 analyzers (Python, Kotlin, Scala, PHP, C#, C++, Go, Swift, Obj-C, Groovy, Rust, JS/TS) have the same silent gap — no inheritance-aware call resolution at all. WI-puluf surfaced the Ruby `include`/`extend` mixin-resolution gap (Sidekiq workers, ActiveModel validations, Rails concerns invisible to the call graph). Per ADR-0003-ext, `linkers/inheritance.py` is the Infrastructure-subcategory linker for `extends`/`implements` edges, but no equivalent linker exists for *call-site* inherited resolution. Pattern: the call-site walk must live alongside `inheritance.py` (call-graph layer), not duplicated inside every analyzer."  # 864b
